# Build output
*.obj
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.map
*.exp
*.lib
*.ilk
*.idb

# A packaged build. The release archive is assembled by .github\workflows\release.yml
# on the runner and published as a release asset -- it is never committed, and a
# hand-made wrlines.zip left in the root is the one piece of build output that
# `git add .` would otherwise sweep into a commit.
*.zip

# Runtime data.
#
# wrlines_data\demos\ holds demos fetched from Momentum's leaderboard, which
# carry other players' names and SteamID64s just as the ones the game
# downloads do.
#
# Not just build noise: wrlines_data\paths\ holds .wrpath files derived from
# other players' downloaded demos, and every one of them carries that player's
# name and SteamID64. They are yours to generate locally, not to publish.
# wrlines.log and wrlines_offsets.ini are per-machine too.
#
# wrlines_data\into_game.txt lists the demos copied into the game's own replay
# folder, and it is the ONLY thing the removal button will delete -- so it is
# per-machine state that must not be shared, and losing it strands those copies
# rather than corrupting anything.
#
# wrlines_data\friends.txt is the SteamID64 of every one of YOUR Steam friends,
# written so the fetch script can ask the leaderboard about them. That is other
# people's identities, in a file, for your convenience -- it does not leave your
# machine except as the ids in that one request, and it must not leave this
# repository at all.
wrlines_data/

# A demo, anywhere, for the same reason: it is a recording of somebody's run
# with their name and SteamID64 in the header. The harnesses write two of these
# under tests\ and delete them again, and a crashed run must not leave one
# behind where `git add .` would find it.
*.mtv

# Third-party trees, cloned by hand -- see README, "Build".
#
# third_party\ is deliberately NOT here: those are committed, because they are a
# few frozen files that decide what a .wrpath contains rather than fifty that
# draw a panel. third_party\VERSION.txt argues it properly.
imgui/
minhook/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Dear ImGui's own settings file. Ours lives in wrlines_data\ -- wr_imgui.cpp
# points io.IniFilename there so the panel remembers where you put it -- but a
# stray copy still turns up in the working tree, and it is per-machine state
# rather than anything to ship.
imgui.ini

# Reference material dropped in to be read, and NOT to be republished.
#
# surf-physics.md is somebody else's write-up of Valve's gamemovement.cpp. It
# carries no licence, and it quotes the Source SDK at length -- so committing it
# to a public MIT repository would be redistributing two things that are not
# ours to redistribute. The same rule the other reference drops already follow by
# living outside the repo entirely (see wrlines-reference\).
#
# What it taught is in docs\how-it-works.md and in the comments on wr_stress.h
# and wr_phase.h, as FACTS and formulas reimplemented from the description --
# the same standard applied to strafe-analyzer and sm-boardstats. The document
# itself stays local.
surf-physics.md

# Editors / IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln
*.vcxproj*
